  "id": "66",
  "name": "Activities auxiliary to financial service and insurance activities",
  "section": "L",
  "summary": "Exchanges, brokers, payment processors, insurance intermediaries and asset managers use AI in trading and execution, market and communications surveillance, payment fraud scoring, advice and research, and increasingly sell AI-enabled data and tools to clients. Filings cite SEC and FINRA positions on predictive data analytics and AI washing, MiFID algorithmic-trading controls and DORA, and flag deepfake and account-takeover fraud, agentic commerce bypassing intermediaries, and fee pressure from AI-native entrants. For asset managers AI is also an investment theme and a concentration risk: AI-themed funds, data-centre and digital-infrastructure strategies, and mega-cap AI valuation exposure.",
